    "answer": {
      "short": "The probabilities must sum to $1$, giving $p=-\\frac15$. Then $P(3)=-\\frac35$ and $P(4)=-\\frac15$, which are negative. Hence this cannot be a probability distribution.",
      "worked": "Suppose this is a probability distribution. Its probabilities must sum to $1$:\n$$\\begin{align*}(2p+1)+(1-p)+3p+p&=1\\\\5p+2&=1\\\\5p&=-1\\\\p&=-\\frac15.\\end{align*}$$\nThen $P(3)=3p=-\\frac35$ and $P(4)=p=-\\frac15$. Probabilities cannot be negative, so this cannot represent a probability distribution.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
